0,Tabasco Nahuatl - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tabasco_Nahuatl,"Tabasco Nahuatl or Nawat of Tabasco is a moribund Nahuan language spoken in Cupilco in the Mexican state of Tabasco.[1]. The language belongs to the eastern branch of the Nahuan language family, and exhibits a number of divergent features.[2][better source needed].","Nahuatl, Tabasco",Uto-Aztecan
